   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Expressing the minimum expectation 「でさえ、ですら、おろか」"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "In this section, we'll learn various ways to express the minimum expectation. This grammar is not used as often as you might think as there are many situations where a simpler expression would sound more natural, but you should still become familiar with it."
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Using 「(で)さえ」 to describe the minimum requirement"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Vocabulary"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "1. 私【わたし】- me; myself; I"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "2. 子供【こ・ども】- child"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "3. 食べる【た・べる】(ru-verb) - to eat"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "4. 行く【い・く】(u-verb) - to go"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "5. 言う【い・う】(u-verb) - to say"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "6. 読む【よ・む】(u-verb) - to read"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "7. 宿題【しゅく・だい】- homework"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "8. 多い【おお・い】(i-adj) - numerous"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "9. トイレ - bathroom; toilet"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "10. 時間【じ・かん】- time"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "11. ある (u-verb) - to exist (inanimate)"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "12. お金【お・かね】- money"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "13. 何【なに〜なん】- what"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "14. 出来る【で・き・る】(ru-verb) - to be able to do"
